# Python environment and caches -- environment-specific / regenerable
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# GENERATED OUTPUT: everything in output/ is ignored, and the handful of files
# worth versioning are named back in one by one (Lode, 2026-08-19).
#
# This started as a deny-list: output/*.html, the R-cut grids, the matrix JSON,
# output/ratio/, each rule written the day that file became a problem. The
# reason for the flip is that a deny-list only knows about the reports that
# already exist. Every new variant report, grid or cache landed
# untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add -A` away from being committed, and
# the rules only caught up after it had already churned a commit.
#
# The test for the list below is unchanged (2026-08-18): does anyone ever need
# to READ this at a past commit? An HTML page is a view of the JSON beside it,
# and the R-cut grids' conclusions live in the audit, so no. What earns a line
# here is the measured RESULT, and only while it stays small. Everything else
# is regenerated by the Update button.
#
# MECHANICS, do not "tidy" this into `output/`: git will not re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so the entry must glob the directory's
# CONTENTS (output/*) or every ! line below goes silently dead. Test any change
# with `git check-ignore -v output/<file>` and `git status --ignored`.
output/*
!output/quickfix1m1dc_all.json
!output/charter_trades_quickfix1m1dc.json
!output/quickfix1m1dc_levels.json
!output/quickfix1m1dc_gc.json
!output/quickfix1m1dc_gc_sweep.json
!output/published_history.jsonl
